metal/build/
metal/iso/boot/outrun-kernel.elf
metal/iso/boot/user_init.elf

# v1.2: built ISOs must not be committed to the repo root.
#
# `outrun-launch-desktop-1.2.0-dev.iso` was uploaded here through the GitHub
# web UI (c583409) as a 13.6 MB blob with no LFS filter behind it, joining four
# older 12 MB images already in the root. Every one of them is permanent: a
# blob in history is downloaded by every future clone whether or not the file
# still exists at HEAD, so the repository only ever gets larger.
#
# It is also the wrong way to share a test image, because a committed artefact
# carries no evidence. `make release-iso` emits the ISO with its MD5 and
# SHA-256 beside it, which is what lets a later run prove which binary it
# booted -- the discipline CLAUDE.md's release protocol exists to enforce.
# Publish images as release assets, not as tracked files.
/*.iso

# v0.78: harness evidence. Gate runs write here rather than into metal/build/,
# so `make clean` cannot destroy the logs that say what happened — which it has
# now done to a reproduction and to an unexplained failure, in that order.
metal/.logs/

# v0.82: Claude Code's per-project directory — local settings, and the
# scratch worktrees it creates. An orphaned 120 MB copy of the tree sat here
# untracked for several releases because nothing ignored it and nothing
# pruned it; `git worktree prune` removes the REGISTRATION, never the files.
.claude/
metal/tools/__pycache__/
